&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;L&#39;équipe Data Platform de DECATHLON recherche ses futur-e-s Développeur-se-s Full Stack basé·e·s à Lille/Paris.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Au cœur de l’entité Decathlon Digital, nous recherchons nos futur.es Développeur·se·s&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Full Stack &lt;/strong&gt;pour rejoindre les équipes Data Factory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cette plateforme technologique, globale à tout le groupe de manière internationale, soutient le développement de l’usage de la Data chez Decathlon, du calcul du chiffre d’affaires à l’aide de conception de produits innovants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nous opérons une Modern Data Stack de pointe, avec un Lakehouse comme centre de gravité. Notre mission ? Garantir la scalabilité, l&#39;automatisation et l&#39;excellence des pratiques de développement pour l&#39;ensemble de nos communautés (Data Engineers, Analysts, Scientists).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ton futur terrain de jeu&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;La Data Factory est organisée en équipes expertes, chacune pilotée par un binôme Tech Lead &amp;amp; Product Manager. Selon ton profil et tes affinités, tu intégreras l’un de nos collectifs :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🎨 Équipe UserXP (User Experience)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tu es l&#39;interface entre la plateforme et ses utilisateurs. Ton rôle est de concevoir des outils et des workflows qui simplifient la vie des développeurs data, en mettant l&#39;accent sur l&#39;ergonomie et l&#39;efficacité opérationnelle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📥 Équipe Ingestion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ton objectif : rendre l&#39;ingestion de données &quot;seamless&quot;. Tu développes et maintiens nos solutions internes (DFI - Data Factory Ingestion) pour garantir un flux de données fluide, normé et automatisé vers le datalake.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;STACK TECHNIQUE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un environnement full cloud (AWS-GCP)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kubernetes, avec full CI/CD (Flux, Github Action...)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;S3, Redshift, PostgreSQL, GCS, BigQuery&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EMR, Databricks, AWS Athena&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Airflow&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Jira/Confluence, GitHub&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Langages : (au moins 2 parmi) : Python, Java, JavaScript/TypeScript&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frameworks/Librairies : React, Angular, Vue.js, Spring, Django, Flask, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TA FUTURE CONTRIBUTION&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tu seras en charge de:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Concevoir, développer et maintenir des composants front-end et back-end de la plateforme data, en mettant l&#39;accent sur l&#39;expérience développeur et l&#39;automatisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribuer à la mise en place d&#39;une plateforme data self-service, en fournissant des outils et des services qui simplifient le développement, le déploiement et l&#39;exploitation des solutions data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Développer des API et des services robustes et évolutifs pour l&#39;accès et la manipulation des données.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implémenter des interfaces utilisateur intuitives pour les outils et services de la plateforme data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automatiser les processus de développement, de test et de déploiement (CI/CD) pour garantir une livraison rapide et fiable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborer étroitement avec les équipes Data Science, Data Engineering et Ops pour comprendre leurs besoins et y répondre efficacement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participer à la veille technologique et proposer des solutions innovantes pour améliorer la plateforme data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apprendre et appliquer les bonnes pratiques de développement logiciel, de test et de documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DECATHLON DIGITAL&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Imaginez si la technologie nous permettait de repousser les frontières et d&#39;offrir des expériences sportives inédites. C&#39;est précisément notre ambition chez Decathlon Digital ! Nous sommes une équipe de plus de 5 000 experts en ingénierie logicielle, gestion de produits, données, cloud et cybersécurité, répartis à Paris, Lille et Amsterdam. Ensemble, nous créons la plus vaste plateforme sportive numérique, en exploitant les innovations technologiques pour optimiser la chaîne de valeur, concevoir des expériences connectées et donner une seconde vie à nos produits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Changeons la donne pour de bon.&lt;/strong&gt; Notre passion du sport nous guide et nous voulons qu’elle perdure. C’est pourquoi nous nous engageons à bâtir un modèle technologique plus durable, en réduisant notre impact direct sur l&#39;environnement, et en créant un espace sûr et inclusif pour apprendre et nous épanouir ensemble. Rejoins l’équipe et façonnons le futur du sport.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt; Find more  English Speaking Jobs in France  on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Intermediate Software Engineer on GitLab’s Vulnerability Management team, you’ll help build the core security workflows that GitLab Ultimate customers use to triage, prioritize, and act on vulnerabilities. You’ll work primarily in Ruby on Rails on backend systems, including security dashboards, vulnerability reports, and ingestion pipelines. You’ll take ownership of well-defined projects, solve technical problems with support from experienced team members, and collaborate with other engineers. You’ll also have opportunities to contribute beyond the backend when the work requires it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join a fullstack team, working together with product managers, designers, and&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/job-families/engineering/development/frontend/&quot;&gt; frontend engineers&lt;/a&gt; to solve problems across the Vulnerability Management domain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop and maintain backend features for GitLab’s vulnerability management workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Confidently ship features and improvements with minimal guidance and support from other team members; collaborate with the team on larger projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Help improve the performance, reliability, and scalability of security data ingestion and reporting systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with frontend engineers and contribute across the stack when needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work with engineers across security teams as vulnerability data and workflows come together in Vulnerability Management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with Product Management and Product Design to maintain a high bar for quality&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Craft code that meets our&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.gitlab.com/development/contributing/style_guides/&quot;&gt; internal standards&lt;/a&gt; for style, maintainability, and best practices for a high-scale web environment&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Conduct code reviews within our&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.gitlab.com/development/code_review/&quot;&gt; Code Review Guidelines&lt;/a&gt; and ensure community contributions receive a swift response&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recognize impediments to our efficiency as a team (&quot;technical debt&quot;), propose and implement solutions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Participate in&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/engineering/on-call/&quot;&gt; on-call rotations&lt;/a&gt; to assist troubleshooting product operations, security operations, and urgent engineering issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience building and maintaining backend applications with Ruby on Rails.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience delivering and maintaining software systems as part of a larger engineering team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ability to investigate technical problems, ask for context when needed, and work toward a practical resolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience working with relational databases such as PostgreSQL.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Clear communication and collaboration skills in a distributed team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An interest in learning from others, sharing knowledge, and growing your technical skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Frontend development experience, including JavaScript or Vue.js, is helpful.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with Elasticsearch, graph databases, vulnerability management, application security, or related transferable skills is helpful.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Vulnerability Management team develops the core security workflows that help GitLab customers triage and manage vulnerabilities. The team owns areas including the security dashboard, vulnerability reports, and ingestion pipelines, and serves as an important interface for security-related features across GitLab. The team is focused on moving beyond lists of findings toward workflows that help customers prioritize and coordinate remediation. You’ll collaborate asynchronously with a small, distributed group and with related security teams, including the Agentic Security Flows team.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt; Find  Jobs in United Kingdom  on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Software Engineer - Industrial Automation, Semiconductor &amp;amp; Scientific Instrumentation (Talent Pool) - all grades&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Private Healthcare (AXA) | 3x Salary Life Assurance | Annual Bonus | EMI Share Scheme | Hybrid Working&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay ranges:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;£32,000 –&amp;nbsp; £50,000&amp;nbsp; (Junior roles)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;£50,000 – £70,000 (Senior roles)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salaries are variable. We will always advise you of the role and pay range which aligns to the role we are considering you for if you are invited to attend an assessment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Abingdon, Oxfordshire&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working Pattern:&lt;/strong&gt; Hybrid (typically 3 days per week onsite)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you a Software Engineer who enjoys building software that controls real-world hardware rather than websites, mobile apps or business systems?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Do you have experience developing software for industrial automation, scientific instrumentation, semiconductor equipment, robotics, machine control, motion systems or other complex engineering products?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At &lt;strong&gt;Infinitesima&lt;/strong&gt;, software engineering sits at the heart of everything we do. Our engineers develop the applications, control systems and operator interfaces that power sophisticated Atomic Force Microscopy (AFM) inspection and metrology systems used by leading semiconductor manufacturers worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we prepare for significant growth over the next 6-12 months, we&#39;re building a network of talented Software Engineers across a range of experience levels, from early-career engineers through to Principal Engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;d love to hear from exceptional engineers who would like to be considered as future opportunities become available.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Infinitesima?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based in Abingdon, Oxfordshire, Infinitesima develops advanced semiconductor metrology technology that is helping enable the next generation of electronics manufacturing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our technology combines cutting-edge software, precision mechanics, motion control and nanoscale measurement science to solve some of the most challenging problems in semiconductor inspection.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a growing team of more than 150 scientists, engineers and business professionals, backed by world-class investors including Applied Ventures, the venture capital arm of Applied Materials, one of the global leaders in semiconductor equipment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to register your interest with a company where software engineering directly influences the performance of highly advanced scientific and industrial systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technologies and Skills We&#39;re Actively Interested In&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re particularly keen to connect with Software Engineers who bring one or more of the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industrial C#/.NET development experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desktop application development using WPF or similar frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with object-oriented programming languages such as C#, Java or C++&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software development for industrial automation, robotics or machine control systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tool control or hardware-integrated software development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Precision motion control, mechatronics or real-time control systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scientific instrumentation, semiconductor equipment or metrology systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working alongside electronics, optics, hardware or mechanical engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional experience that would be advantageous includes:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;C++ development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Messaging and communication technologies such as DDS, MQTT, RabbitMQ, ZeroMQ or Named Pipes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agile software delivery and sprint-based development environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Future Software Engineering Opportunities Could Involve&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depending on the role and level, future opportunities could include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing and developing C#/.NET applications for semiconductor inspection and metrology systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing software that controls precision motion systems and nanoscale positioning technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building user interfaces and HMI applications using WPF and related technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrating software with motion controllers, piezo actuators, sensors and data acquisition hardware&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting system integration, verification, validation and software releases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to software architecture, engineering standards and best practice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating within multidisciplinary teams spanning software, electronics, optics and mechanical engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentoring and supporting less experienced engineers (senior-level roles)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Interested In&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re particularly interested in hearing from engineers who have experience in one or more of the following environments:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industrial automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motion control systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Robotics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scientific instrumentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Semiconductor equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Metrology systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manufacturing automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Control systems engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High-precision electromechanical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and development environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For early-career engineers, a strong academic background in computer science, software engineering, mathematics, physics or another scientific discipline is highly valuable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more experienced engineers, experience within scientific, engineering or hardware-focused industries would be particularly relevant.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This Talent Pool May Be a Good Fit If...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve developed software that interacts with hardware, instruments or machinery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve worked in engineering environments rather than purely commercial software settings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy solving complex technical challenges involving software, electronics and mechanical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re excited by the idea of contributing to advanced semiconductor technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This Talent Pool Is Less Likely to Be Suitable If...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Your experience is primarily focused on web development&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Your background is predominantly SaaS, fintech or e-commerce platforms&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;You have limited exposure to hardware-integrated software or engineering products&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re interested in candidates who have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Physics or a related discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;OR&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equivalent commercial experience developing complex engineering software systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join Our Talent Community&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re interested in future Software Engineering opportunities at Infinitesima, we&#39;d encourage you to apply and introduce yourself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Future positions are expected to span multiple levels, from Software Engineer through to Principal Engineer, with compensation and responsibilities aligned to experience, capability and scope of role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By joining our Software Engineer Talent Pool, you&#39;ll be among the first professionals we consider when suitable opportunities become available. Whilst applying does not guarantee an interview or future position, it allows us to contact you directly when a role aligns with your skills and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exceptional engineering needs exceptional engineers. If you&#39;re ready for your next challenge, we&#39;d love to stay connected.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Infinitesima is a privately owned company founded in 2001 as a spin-out from the University of Bristol by CTO Professor Andrew Humphris.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our scientists and engineers are dedicated to enabling the next generation of semiconductor devices through the development of innovative metrology solutions used by customers around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that diversity of thought, background and experience drives innovation. We are committed to creating an inclusive environment where everyone can contribute, develop and succeed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you require adjustments at any stage of the recruitment process, please let us know and we&#39;ll do our best to support you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Recruitment Journey&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interview availability:&lt;/strong&gt; Monday to Friday, 9:00am to 4:30pm UK time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stage 1&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;45-minute remote interview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An opportunity to discuss your experience, technical background and career interests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stage 2&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Onsite interview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A collaborative assessment of technical capability, communication style, problem-solving approach and ways of working. You&#39;ll also have the opportunity to learn more about our technology, culture and future plans.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re committed to creating a comfortable interview experience. If eye contact feels challenging, please let us know. For remote interviews, you&#39;re welcome to switch your camera off after introductions if that helps you feel more at ease.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We dress casually and informal attire is absolutely fine for onsite interviews.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;N.B. Depending on operational requirements, we may invite you to a group assessment where several vacancies are available. In this instance, full details of how the day will be for you, salary and job description will be shared when you are invited.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Note on How We Use AI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We use AI solely to transcribe interviews so that interviewers can focus on the conversation rather than taking detailed notes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is not used to assess candidates or make hiring decisions. All recruitment decisions are made by people based on the conversations and evidence gathered throughout the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location and Working Pattern&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We recognise the value of flexibility and offer hybrid working wherever possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Most employees typically work onsite three days per week, although some positions may require additional onsite presence due to the nature of the work and business needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Recruitment agencies: Infinitesima only works with approved recruitment partners and does not accept unsolicited CVs. Please do not submit candidate details in response to this advertisement. Infinitesima is not responsible for any fees relating to unsolicited applications or CV submissions.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
